<title>CHINA: HK stocks extend slide in afternoon on HK dlr fears.</title>
<headline>HK stocks extend slide in afternoon on HK dlr fears.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong stocks extended their losses in Friday afternoon trade with the blue chip Hang Seng Index sliding 309 points, or 1.88 percent, to 16,187 as selling increased on jitters over the Hong Kong dollar.  </p>
<p>HSBC fell HK$5.00 to HK$272 and Hang Seng Bank lost HK$3.00 to HK$104.50.</p>
<p>Cheung Kong eased HK$2.00 to HK$92.25 and Hutchison was down HK$2.50 to HK$78.75. -- Alison Leung, Newsroom (852) 2843 6369</p>
</text>
